# Prime assessment handoff — 2026-10-25

Status: review material, not an executable released pack.
Page: 10.10.12.rebuild / 1001.assessment.

The Director asked Codex to reassess whether the rebuild is becoming functional and record its issues for Prime. Read 04.md, then evidence/probes.json and the relevant source sections. 05.01.md is the open review queue. Do not treat its blank replies as release instructions.

What advanced: six selected suites pass; loader, face/section operations, import/seating, pack/return lifecycle, saved resume state, timer, user words, and PDF experiments exist.

What blocks confidence: a negative readiness fixture passes; boot still routes to the old work book; current contents omit the queue and recent work; loader is unseated; candidate and working kernel/checker contracts are not aligned; component cold-process tests are being used where a complete cold workflow is needed.

Your next useful output is a short evidence-based response to F01–F05, not another general architecture essay. Mark each finding reproduced, closed with evidence, intentionally deferred with its authority, or disputed with a counterexample. Preserve Director decisions. Identify already-authorized work separately from new decisions. Prepare the smallest released repair slices through the existing dev/pack/return process.

Respect the October 24 decision in 0417.pack-lint/06.02.md: lint requests promotion; the Director promotes. This assessment does not grant auto-promotion. Missing intentionally held face law is not an instruction to fill it.

Proposed milestone: from the declared checkout and entry, a fresh worker can find the current work, run one useful task through compute, preserve its decision and result, close its bounded work under the applicable authority, and resume it in another process. Report every remembered path or manual bypass. Until this passes, describe the result as functional prototype tools with incomplete integration.

An assessment response does not authorize modifying source code. A released repair needs its own cited scope. No commit or merge is requested by this handoff.
